cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Slurm Workload Manager
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the metadata from this file when
  you refer to it in publications or re-use, adapt, or expand on
  the material in your own teaching.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Clemens
    family-names: Lange
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3632-3157
abstract: >-
  A hands-on introduction to using the Slurm workload manager on a shared
  Linux cluster. The lesson covers cluster discovery, batch and interactive
  jobs, monitoring and diagnosis, resource requests and accounting, and job
  arrays, with optional extensions on efficient campaigns and scheduler
  mechanics.
